# Database & API Design

## PostgreSQL Rules
- Use NUMERIC(10,2) for all monetary values — never FLOAT or DOUBLE
- Use ENUM or CHECK constraint for OS status column; valid values: RECEBIDA, EM_DIAGNOSTICO, AGUARDANDO_APROVACAO, EM_EXECUCAO, FINALIZADA, ENTREGUE, RECUSADA
- Apply foreign key constraints with referential integrity for: veiculo→cliente, os→cliente, os→veiculo, os_servico→os, os_servico→servico, os_peca→os, os_peca→peca, customer→user
- Many-to-many: `USER_ROLE` table linking user↔role
- Index columns: customer.cpf, customer.cnpj, veiculo.placa, os.status, os.cliente_id, user.email
- Use database transactions (BEGIN/COMMIT) for: OS creation with parts, stock decrement, status transitions
- Use SELECT FOR UPDATE when reading stock quantity before decrement

## Migration Strategy
- All schema changes via versioned migration files (never alter schema manually)
- Migration files named: `V{version}__{description}.sql` (Flyway) or numeric prefix (other tools)
- Never drop or modify existing columns in a migration — add new columns, deprecate old ones

## API Design (RESTful)
### Endpoints Overview
- `POST   /auth/login` — obtain JWT (public)
- `GET    /os/:id/status` — client tracking (public, no auth)
- `POST   /clientes` — create client (ADMIN, ATENDENTE)
- `GET    /clientes` — list clients (ADMIN, ATENDENTE)
- `GET    /clientes/:id` — get client (ADMIN, ATENDENTE)
- `PUT    /clientes/:id` — update client (ADMIN, ATENDENTE)
- `DELETE /clientes/:id` — delete client (ADMIN)
- Same CRUD pattern for `/veiculos`, `/servicos`, `/pecas`
- `POST   /os` — create OS (ADMIN, ATENDENTE)
- `GET    /os` — list OS with filters: status, cliente_id, veiculo_id (ADMIN, ATENDENTE, MECANICO)
- `GET    /os/:id` — full OS detail with services, parts, values, status history (ADMIN, ATENDENTE, MECANICO)
- `PATCH  /os/:id/status` — advance OS status (ADMIN, ATENDENTE, MECANICO)
- `POST   /os/:id/approve` — CLIENTE approves own budget → EM_EXECUCAO
- `POST   /os/:id/reject` — CLIENTE rejects own budget → RECUSADA
- `GET    /relatorios/tempo-medio` — average execution time report (ADMIN, ATENDENTE)
- `POST   /usuarios` — create user (ADMIN only)
- `PUT    /usuarios/:id/roles` — update user roles (ADMIN only)

## Request / Response Conventions
- All request and response bodies in JSON
- Dates and timestamps in ISO 8601 format (UTC)
- IDs as UUIDs
- Pagination on list endpoints: `?page=1&limit=20`, response includes `total`, `page`, `limit`, `data`
- Filter parameters on GET /os: `?status=EM_EXECUCAO&cliente_id=...&veiculo_id=...`

## Swagger/OpenAPI
- Every endpoint must have: summary, description, request body schema, response schemas (success + errors)
- Tag endpoints by domain: Clientes, Veiculos, Servicos, Pecas, OrdemDeServico, Relatorios, Auth, Usuarios
- Document 401/403 responses on all protected endpoints
- Mark public OS status endpoint explicitly as requiring no authentication
- Document role requirements for each protected endpoint
